If your character is prepared to deal with the Wizard and
the large swarms of enemies in the Sanctum, being
surrounded should in general not be much of a problem,
unless you remain surrounded for a long time or are
surrounded by exceptionally dangerous foes.

> I didn't have conflict,

Conflict is widely considered desirable in the late game,
although personally I tend to prefer to spend my ring slots
on slow digestion and either regeneration or levitation.

Still, if you _don't_ have conflict, you need another way
of dealing with large hostile crowds.

Some roles can manage by melee.  This is a particularly
viable option for roles that can use two good weapons.

Some roles can use spells, if they have good ones and can
get 0% failure rates on them.  Charm monster is very useful
if there's anything around you with a low monster-MR, even
if that's not what's threatening you, because every monster
you tame gives your other enemies something to attack
besides you.  Some players keep cursed scrolls of genocide
around so they can produce swarms of relatively strong
monsters with low MR that they can then tame.  (Purple
worms are a common favorite for this.)  Attack spells can
also be a recipe for success.

Multi-fire projectiles can also be good, as they allow you
to get in more hits per turn than melee.  Roles that can
get expert in dagger should carry a nice stack of blessed
+6 or +7 elvish daggers if possible.  Some roles may need
to use a bow instead, although switching between that and a
melee weapon uses up time.

Wands of teleport can also be effective, but you may need
several of them.

